			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825964">
									

<p>Good evening beautiful people. I'll be using the handle Influrrno (Before you ask, yes, I came up with that because I like fire and ice motifs just a little too much, and yes, my writing will probably reflect that).</p>
<p>I've only recently been exposed to SCP, but I've always been taken in by unconventional writing formats that breed creativity, so I've been reading up on my skips and tales over the past few months and having a good time.</p>
<p>My ideas for writing SCPs and tales are&#8230; well, I'm pretty sure they're mostly a complete mess conceptually (let's just say I have an idea relating to a steel cable that puts holes in people but also its own plot), but I consider myself at least competent in technical writing style, so we'll have to see how this goes. I'm extremely excited to get and give productive feedback, as I'm a strong believer in improvement by acknowledging your own shortcomings.</p>
<p>To answer the forum's question, my classical element would definitely be Earth. I'd like to think that's because I'm steadfast, consistent and solid, but I suspect it's more because I just don't like to move much.</p>
<p>Anyway, hopefully I end up contributing something interesting to the site, or failing that, a bit of friendliness. Cheers mates!</p>

							</div>

								
					
